[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] 6. **Create a GitHub Actions workflow that automatically runs and tests the program on every push and pull request**
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] ## Expected Output
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] When the program runs, it should output:
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] ```
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] Hello, World!
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] ```
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] ## GitHub Actions Requirements
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] The CI/CD workflow should:
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Set up the appropriate Rust runtime/compiler
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Run the Hello World program
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Verify the output is exactly "Hello, World!"
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Show a green check mark when tests pass
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] 
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] Example workflow structure:
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Checkout code
[2026-09-27T15:16:10.987Z] [STDERR] - Setup Rust environment
